      "id": "claim_4b1b5a6d4e824c179cf3c7a923958575",
      "statement": "The block-level merge policy is enforced by the Master's single DiskManagerInner mutex rather than per-block locks: disjoint byte offsets merge in place, overlapping offsets are last-writer-wins, and compressed writes use multi-frame append or read-modify-recompress.",
