        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a6f0b0a21e78458cb9ee405a4c59f25b",
      "statement": "BoundedInodeCache uses Second-Chance (Clock) eviction: each cached inode has an atomic referenced bit set on cache hit (Relaxed ordering). When capacity is reached, eviction walks a queue, giving referenced entries a second chance (clears bit, re-queues) and evicts only unreferenced entries. Only a single entry is evicted per overflow (not the entire cache).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/disk/caches.rs#L280-L340",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:692c252458e206cb0323299171a0d58121f6bae2d00b9907da541ddc96905b29:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/disk/caches.rs#L354-L423",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7dde4a48377d490ef5c37ed201cff909d1586d22e1a91c2d28aed404cb342367:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_13c63a4a86094241b0ad4b301d761b33",
      "statement": "Write operations (write_data_with_filters) execute in three stages: Stage 1 acquires a shared read lock for inspection and metadata collection then drops it; Stage 2 performs CPU-bound filter/compress/encrypt work with zero locks held; Stage 3 acquires the exclusive write lock only for block allocation and metadata commit, then releases it before flushing via sync_mutex. Concurrent readers are never blocked by compression/encryption CPU work.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/disk.rs#L5671-L5850",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3018464206ec57cc854cf5e345d35f42ee3a593eb144a475fe996634f0c5e9f9:"
